From: leerep <leerep@163.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] init: export saved_command_line

The QSDK 14.0 qca-nss-dp driver sizes its EDMA rings from the
"mem-profile=" boot argument, i.e. from the kernel command line:

	nss_dp_mem_profile_detect() -> __get_mem_profile_flag(saved_command_line)

and it is built as a module, so the symbol has to be exported.  QSDK's 6.6
tree does exactly this (init/main.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL(saved_command_line)), our
vanilla 6.6.88 does not.

Without the boot argument the driver falls back to the HIGH profile
(rx_ring 4096 / tx_ring 2048), which is what the board used before the driver
bump, so exporting the symbol keeps the behaviour identical.

--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -141,6 +141,7 @@ void (*__initdata late_time_init)(void);
 /* Untouched saved command line (eg. for /proc) */
 char *saved_command_line __ro_after_init;
 unsigned int saved_command_line_len __ro_after_init;
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(saved_command_line);
 /* Command line for parameter parsing */
 static char *static_command_line;
 /* Untouched extra command line */
-- 
